# Copy to .env.local and fill in (Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API).
# Leave empty to run the demo: the built-in invented door list and the demo sync server (npm run sync-server).
# With both set, staff sign in with their AAFE account and the door list comes from Supabase; the build then
# carries no door list at all. The anon key is public by design; never put the service_role key here
# (the build guard refuses it).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<PROJECT-REF>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon public key>
# Which copy this build is: "nightly" in the nightly folder shows a "Nightly · test copy" label on every screen and
# in the tab title. Leave it out on stable (AAFE and Demo Day see no label). The build checks it against
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL: the nightly project without it, or any other build with it, is refused.
# VITE_APP_LINE=nightly
